# An emblem is no permanent (CR 114.4), so "a triggered ability of a permanent you control" (CR 603.2d) does not reach its
# abilities. Bot1 plays Chandra, Torch of Defiance and Veyran, Voice of Duality on turn 1, takes Chandra to 7 loyalty and
# on turn 7 gets her emblem ("Whenever you cast a spell, this emblem deals 5 damage to any target"). Then Bot1 casts
# Lightning Bolt at Bot2: Veyran's magecraft, a permanent's ability, triggers twice (Veyran 4/4, the control), and the
# emblem's ability once: Bot2 takes 3 + 5, not 3 + 10.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Chandra, Torch of Defiance
Veyran, Voice of Duality
Lightning Bolt
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chandra, Torch of Defiance.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Chandra, Torch of Defiance.Activate(Ability: Add {R}{R})
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Veyran, Voice of Duality.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Chandra, Torch of Defiance.Activate(Ability: Add {R}{R})
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Chandra, Torch of Defiance.Activate(Ability: Add {R}{R})
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Chandra, Torch of Defiance.Counters.Loyalty = 7
Bot1.Battlefield.Chandra, Torch of Defiance.Activate(Ability: emblem)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Emblems.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Triggers(Veyran gets; Veyran gets; this emblem deals 5)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
? Stack.Count = 4
[T7 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 12
Bot1.Battlefield.Veyran, Voice of Duality.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Veyran, Voice of Duality.Toughness = 4
